1
00:00:00,330 --> 00:00:03,687
Today we continue our series on ecology

2
00:00:03,687 --> 00:00:10,880
and conservation with a look at a particularly endangered member of the black bear family.

3
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:14,330
One in ten black bears is actually born

4
00:00:14,330 --> 00:00:21,660
with a white coat which is the result of a special gene that surfaces in a few.

5
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:25,380
Local people have named it the spirit bear.

6
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:28,740
And according to the legends of these communities

7
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:33,080
its snowy fur brings with it a special power.

8
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:38,540
Because of this, it has always been highly regarded by them

9
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:43,390
so much that they do not speak of seeing it to anyone else.

10
00:00:43,390 --> 00:00:48,090
It is their way of protecting it when strangers visit the area.

11
00:00:48,090 --> 00:00:51,560
The white bear's habitat is quite interesting.

12
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:58,460
The bear's strong relationship with the old- growth rainforest is a complex one.

13
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:05,610
The white bear relies on the huge centuries-old trees in the forest in many ways.

14
00:01:05,610 --> 00:01:16,420
For example, the old-growth trees have extremely long roots that help prevent erosion of the soil along the banks of the many fish streams.

15
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:21,926
Keeping these banks intact is important because these streams are home to salmon,

16
00:01:21,926 --> 00:01:24,890
which are the bear's main food source.

17
00:01:24,890 --> 00:01:30,860
In return, the bear's feeding habits nurture the forest.

18
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:33,492
As the bears eat the salmon,

19
00:01:33,492 --> 00:01:40,950
they discard the skin and bones in great amounts on the forest floor, which provide vital nutrients.

20
00:01:40,950 --> 00:01:48,244
These produce lush vegetation that sustains thousands of other types of life forms,

21
00:01:48,244 --> 00:01:51,610
from birds to insects and more.

22
00:01:51,610 --> 00:01:59,920
Today, the spirit bear lives off the coast of the province of British Columbia on a few islands.

23
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:03,300
There is great concern for their survival

24
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:08,890
since it is estimated that less than two hundred of these white bears remain.

25
00:02:08,890 --> 00:02:21,938
The best way to protect them is to make every effort to preserve the delicate balance of their forest environment -

26
00:02:21,938 --> 00:02:25,200
in other words, their ecosystem.

27
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:30,610
The greatest threat to the bear's existence is the loss of its habitat.

28
00:02:30,610 --> 00:02:38,760
Over many years, logging companies have stripped the land by cutting down a large number of trees.

29
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:41,460
In addition, they have built roads

30
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:45,913
which have fractured the areas where the bear usually feeds,

31
00:02:45,913 --> 00:02:49,490
and many hibernation sites have also been lost.

32
00:02:49,490 --> 00:02:56,540
The logging of the trees along the streams has damaged the places where the bears fish.

33
00:02:56,540 --> 00:03:01,854
To make matters worse, the number of salmon in those streams is declining

34
00:03:01,854 --> 00:03:06,350
because there is no legal limit on fishing at the moment.

35
00:03:06,350 --> 00:03:13,063
All these influences have a negative impact on the spirit bear's very existence,

36
00:03:13,063 --> 00:03:23,390
which is made all the more fragile by the fact that reproduction among these bears has always been disappointingly low.

37
00:03:23,390 --> 00:03:27,690
And so, what's the situation going forward?

38
00:03:27,690 --> 00:03:36,780
Community organizations, environmental groups and the British Columbia government are now working together on the problem.

39
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:43,240
The government is now requiring logging companies to adopt a better logging method

40
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:45,380
which is a positive step.

41
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:55,170
However, these measures alone may not be sufficient to ensure a healthy population of the spirit bear in the future.

42
00:03:55,170 --> 00:03:58,460
Other steps also need to be taken

43
00:03:58,860 --> 00:04:02,776
While it is important to maintain the spirit bear's habitat,

44
00:04:02,776 --> 00:04:07,250
there also needs to be more emphasis on its expansion.

45
00:04:07,250 --> 00:04:15,300
The move is justified as it will also create space for other bears that are losing their homes...?
